BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Metrotrails Hiking
UID:event_315880667@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260731T040159Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260823T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260823T180000
SUMMARY:Shawangunks Loop Hike
DESCRIPTION:Metrotrails: NJ\, PA\, NY Metropolitan Area Hiking and More!\n
 Join us for this interesting loop hike in the Shawangunks of New York!\nFo
 r this 15 mile loop trip\, we will meet at the Foordmore Trailhead for the
  Long Path near Kerkhonksen New York.\nThe most difficult parts will be th
 e very beginning where we ascend the Shawangunk Ridge on backroads and the
  Stony Kill Carriageway.\nOnce we reach the top of the ridge\, we continue
  a bit through the blueberry lands\, and then descend a bit on Smiley Carr
 iageway. There will be one rough bit of trail down to a waterfall\, and th
 en more pleasant back roads. There is one bit that has metal rungs to clim
 b up\, but it is quite short. I'll be prepared with a pack to carry all of
  Ev's stuff for this stretch.\nThe only regular road walk stuff is pretty 
 much at the very beginning\, and the beginning of the ascent.\nOnce we do 
 the entire ridge bit\, two thirds of the hike\, we'll make our way onto th
 e Delaware and Hudson Canal\, as well as the O&W Rail Trail.\nThis will pr
 ovide us with an easy creekside walk for the last stretch.\nApart from two
  difficult miles\, the rest of the hike should be very relaxing.\nThe grad
 ual climb will be on back road and dirt road\, and then trail. After that\
 , we have ten miles of gradual downhill to flat.\nThere are going to be a 
 few stores in Ellenville at mile 11 or 12\, but otherwise there are no oth
 er stores along the way.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/metrotrails/events/315880667/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260728T221453Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260728T221453Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Metrotrails Hiking
UID:event_315884527@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260731T040159Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260830T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260830T230000
SUMMARY:Brandywine Hike
DESCRIPTION:Metrotrails: NJ\, PA\, NY Metropolitan Area Hiking and More!\n
 Join us for this point to point 15 mile hike\, the next in the Brandywine 
 Series!\nThis time\, we'll travel between Delacy Soccer Complex in East Br
 adford Township and Downingtown.\nWe already covered some of Downingtown p
 reviously\, but this time we'll cover some other municipal trails and form
 er route of the Brandywine Trail near the beginning\, as well as the end o
 f Struble Trail\, Lions Trail\, and we'll trace the historic route of the 
 Pennsylvania Railroad New Holland Branch briefly.\nFrom here\, we take som
 e new creekside trails\, and then make our way on the Brandywine Trail up 
 to the Philadelphia and Thorndale Branch. We take another municipal trail 
 from here south to a pleasant back road with no lines in it\, and then rev
 isit the Harmony Hill Covered Bridge.\nAlong this stretch\, we'll follow t
 he alternate Brandywine Trail we saw previously\, out to Sugar's Bridge.\n
 From here\, the Brandywine Trail follows a pleasant back road bit down to 
 the Natural Land Trust Stroud Preserve.\nWe will hike the Stroud Preserve 
 trails that we'd not explored before\, then make our way south along Brand
 ywine Trail to Jeffers Ford.\nAnother brief road walk leads us to another 
 foot path section\, then a short back road to an abandoned road which will
  lead us down to our end point.\nThe only place we pass any store on this 
 one is in Downingtown near the beginning\, so everyone should come prepare
 d with all they need!\nIf needed\, contact me at 908 343 8374
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/metrotrails/events/315884527/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260729T031454Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260729T031454Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
